0.2376.543This is a continuation-in-part application and claims priority to U.S. Patent Application No. 18/445825 entitled "Automated Allergy Office System and Method" (Prince and Novak) filed on 2024-02-22; and a divisional application and claims priority to U.S. Patent Application No. 18/078856 entitled "Automated Allergy Office System and Method" (Prince and Novak) filed on 2022-12-09, now U.S. Patent No. 11911172 issued on 2024-02-28; and a continuation-in-part application and claims priority to U.S. Patent Application No. 17/992125 entitled "Methods for Administering Multiple Allergens" (Prince) filed on 2022-11-22, now U.S. Patent No. 11696722 issued on 2023-07-11; and a continuation-in-part application and claims priority to U.S. Patent Application No. 17/468132 entitled "Multiple Test Applicator" (Prince) filed on 2021-09-07, now U.S. Patent No. 11369782 issued on 2022-06-28; and a continuation-in-part application and claims priority to U.S. Patent Application No. 17/402413 entitled "Multiple Allergen Test Method Applicator" (Prince) filed on 2021-08-13, now U.S. Patent No. 11517249 issued on 2022-12-06; and a continuation-in-part application and claims priority to U.S. Provisional Application No. 63/289350 entitled "Automated Allergy Office System and Method" (Prince) filed on 2021-12-14.

