0.2336.543includes means for retesting negative test results. The retesting of the negative test results is performed using prefilled vials and syringes, wherein the augmented reality headset, smart phone or computer tablet, monitors the content of each vial and instructs the nurse where to perform the subcutaneous retest. Each vial is equipped with an electronic tag that contains information on the vial contents, its temperature history, its expiration date, the volume in the vial, along with other information such as the manufacturer's name and its dilution percentage.    This information is programmed into the electronic tag or label, by a trained technician, in the doctor's office.

